Anaerobic digestion is being extensively used for the treatment of high strength wastewaters like landfill leachate because it has significant advantages i.e., lesser energy requirement and biogas production [26]. Biogas is also effective in promoting the concept of circular economy, which is based on reuse and recycling and may become the solution for resource crisis leading to sustainability [27]. Biogas is having various practical applications such as: (i) It can be utilized for the onsite generation of heat and power by using ‘combined heat and power’ (CHP) engines; (ii) It can be used as green alternative for natural gas; (iii) It can be used as substrate in fuel cells [28]. If the biogas production drops abruptly, it is an indicator that other process parameters like VA and pH may have changed and can lead to anaerobic digester system upset. A bubble counter having innovative design equipped with state of art regulator and an optical digital sensor that can measure biogas production was used in this study. Gas produced from the MABR was captured and measured in litre per day. Initially the bubble counter is calibrated then gas produced was captured and passed through a unique device (regulator) to produce uniform bubbles. Bubble counter is shown in Fig. 5
                        . Detected number of bubbles are digitally displayed on the electronic circuit. When the HRT is reduced, there is a hike in the values of gas production (Fig. 6
                        ) and the trend of increment of biogas is seen while increasing the values of OLR. The overall biogas production in the reactor was 0.1, 0.15, 0.32 and 0.4 L/day was observed at different and increasing values of OLR as shown in the figure also the trendline signifies the increase in the biogas production. This shows the stable behavior of MABR system during the anaerobic treatment of landfill leachate containing heavy metals. As it is known that the presence of heavy metals may lead to the reduction of the biogas production [29].
